</section></score></mdiv></body>
<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Brought safely by His hand thus far,</l><l>Why wilt thou now give place to fear?</l><l>How canst thou want if He provide,</l><l>Or lose thy way with such a Guide?</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>When first before His mercy-seat</l><l>Thou didst to Him thine all commit;</l><l>He gave thee warrant from that hour</l><l>To trust His wisdom, love, and power.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Did ever trouble yet befall,</l><l>And He refuse to hear thy call?</l><l>And has He not His promise passed,</l><l>That thou shalt overcome at last?</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>He who has helped me hitherto</l><l>Will help me all my journey through,</l><l>And give me daily cause to raise</l><l>New Ebenezers to His praise.</l></lg>
<lg label="6."><l>Though rough and thorny be the road,</l><l>It leads thee on, apace, to God;</l><l>Then count thy present trials small,</l><l>For God will make amends for all.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
